From ced107eb7a78fe609d96990cb81c92ea8cc234fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:31:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/61] Vulkan on Switch: upload textures through a linear
 image and the 3D engine.

NVK exposes a single queue family with the compute bit on the GM20B and then
implements vkCmdCopyBufferToImage with an internal compute shader. Texture
uploads now write the pixels into a host-visible linear image (unified
memory, no staging buffer) and vkCmdBlitImage it into the tiled texture,
which NVK does with a 3D meta draw. Falls back to vkCmdCopyBufferToImage when
the format has no linear blit support. Used for hardware textures and
post-process textures; rd_vk_blitupload 0 restores the old path.

In Ryujinx, which cannot run NVK's internal compute shaders, this is what
turns the black Vulkan picture into the rendered map (evidence/ryujinx/
32-vk-freedoom). ZVulkan's ImageBuilder gains InitialLayout().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
